Emit OSC 8 hyperlinks from the VT formatter.

Upstream emits hyperlinks for HTML only (its own comment calls VT support
future work). `Terminal::dump_vt` is hmux's compositor primitive -- the bytes
an attached client's terminal receives -- so without this a linked cell
reaches the client as plain text.

The hunks, and what pins each one (all in ghostty-sys/src/lib.rs unless noted):

  1. Close an open link before the row's newline. The compositor splits a dump
     on newlines and repaints each row at its own position, so a link left
     open would carry into whatever is drawn next, including another pane's
     row. HTML keeps one <a> across newlines, so this is VT-only.
     -> vt_dump_closes_osc8_hyperlinks_at_every_row_end
  2. Let the slow path's hyperlink block run for any styled format, not just
     HTML.  -> vt_dump_carries_osc8_hyperlinks
  3. Read the explicit OSC 8 id and pass it to the open sequence; implicit ids
     stay out of the output.  -> vt_dump_carries_osc8_explicit_id
  4. Same id through the point-map's discarding writer, so byte accounting
     matches the real writer.  -> "Page VT hyperlink" (zig, point-map length)
  5. Let the batched cell-run fast path break on hyperlink transitions for any
     styled format. Without this the run swallows the transition and no OSC 8
     is emitted at all -- the trap that survived the previous upstream bump
     unnoticed.  -> vt_dump_separates_adjacent_osc8_hyperlinks
  6/7. The VT arms of formatHyperlinkOpen/Close.
  8. Zig-side tests for the above.

